# /hm:spec — what, why, and how to verify

`/hm:spec <slug>` turns a task into acceptance criteria; it is the only interview. Write files in English; talk to the user in `{{ config.locale }}`.

{{ hm.cli() }}

{{ hm.choices() }}{{ hm.preflight("spec") }}

## Step 0 — Skip check

Skip the interview only when all four hold: one file or config; acceptance obvious from the title; no API, IPC, schema or file-format change; reversible within an hour with no user impact. Then write a minimal SPEC (Intent, one Given-When-Then scenario, Verification), the reason under Refinement Decisions, `irreversible_decisions: []`. Only a non-code change may write `ac: []`; a code change gets one testable AC, because the gate fails `ac: []` beside code. Stamp it without asking: `hm spec_machine approve --yaml specs/SPEC-<slug>.machine.yaml --exempt`.

## Step 0.5 — Intent

Run `hm intent status --json`. With no `active` or `proposed` intent, print `[intent] none`; otherwise ask with {{ hm.ask() }} which one this task serves (each id and title, plus "none"). Step 3 writes `intent: <id>`.

## Step 1 — Prior work

Grep `specs/SPEC-*.md` and `work-docs/PLAN-*.md` for key terms; run `hm memory_retrieve --topic "<topic>"`. Read `work-docs/RESEARCH-<slug>.md` if it exists.

## Step 2 — Interview
{% if _depth != 'minimal' %}
<!-- @hm:comprehension:brief -->
**Design brief, before round 1:** what research or a prior SPEC settled, the ACs you can draft now (provisional), and which of the six categories are open, answered or defaulted (with why). One screen.
{% endif %}
Ask with {{ hm.ask() }}, batching independent questions; always offer "Other — let me describe". From round 2, one question per round offers **"Approve this SPEC and end interview"**: the DRI's acceptance and the only approval (silence never counts). Interview length is your judgment: stop when every slot below is settled, when the DRI approves, or after `interview.main_loop.max_rounds` ({{ _rounds if _rounds else 'unlimited' }}) rounds.

The six categories, in order, skipping settled ones: 1. **Intent** (why now); 2. **Outcomes** ("done", observably); 3. **In-scope scenarios** (2–4 Given-When-Then: normal, edge, failure); 4. **Non-goals**; 5. **Constraints** (the test framework is mandatory); 6. **Verification** (each scenario → unit, integration or manual).

**Oracle, for every AC.** Ask for `oracle_source` (golden, differential, property, rubric or consensus; a property also needs `input_domain`, `transformation`, `expected_relation`) and `oracle_evidence`: why it is independent of the code. "The test will check it" is circular; reject it.

**Irreversible decisions.** What cannot be cheaply undone: schema/file format/storage layout, public API/CLI contract, data migration, security/permission boundary, new external dependency. Each is `{id: IRR-NNN, decision, category, rationale, source: spec}`; `irreversible_decisions: []` is valid.

At most {{ _cap }} open-ended follow-up(s) per turn (closed ones are unlimited), each only when its answer changes the SPEC.
{% if _depth != 'minimal' %}
<!-- @hm:comprehension:round_state -->
**Round state.** Open each round after the first with `## Interview Round {N}`, the decisions locked so far, the delta since the last round ("no change since last round" when none), and the one ambiguity this round resolves and why.
{% endif %}
{%- if _depth == 'deep' %}
<!-- @hm:comprehension:decision_depth -->
**Per-question envelope.** For each question: what it decides, which sections each option rewrites, your recommended option and why, and what undoing it later costs (minutes, a phase, a migration).

<!-- @hm:comprehension:teach_back -->
**Closing readback.** Before ending, restate the locked design in the user's terms: what is built, in what order, what was rejected and why. It needs no reply and gates nothing.
{% endif %}
## Step 3 — Write the SPEC

Write `specs/SPEC-<slug>.md`. Frontmatter: `type: spec`, `task_slug`, `status`, `created`, `tags`, `test_framework`, `interview_rounds`, `intent` (if picked), `summary`. Sections: Intent; Outcomes; In-Scope Scenarios (S1…); Non-Goals; Constraints (table); Irreversible Decisions (table, or "none"); Acceptance Criteria, each `### AC-NNN: <title>`; Verification (scenario, mode, test); Open Questions; Refinement Decisions.

## Step 3.5 — Write the machine.yaml

`specs/SPEC-<slug>.machine.yaml`:
```yaml
schema_version: 3
spec_slug: <slug>
verification_tier: 1
irreversible_decisions: []
ac:
  - id: AC-001
    title: <the heading's title>
    type: mechanical   # parametric | property | judgment
    executable_predicate: <python expression>    # mechanical
    golden_table: [{input: {}, expected: null}]  # parametric
    rubric_id: <id>    # judgment, + judgment_subject_paths
    pending_test: true
    oracle_source: golden
    oracle_evidence: <why it is independent>
```

Every non-judgment AC gets a test; `/hm:execute` writes it and binds `test_ids`.

## Step 4 — Check

Run `hm spec_machine check --all --yaml specs/SPEC-<slug>.machine.yaml --md specs/SPEC-<slug>.md --strictness {{ _strict }}`. It validates, cross-validates and scores. On exit 1, fix and rerun once; if it still fails, report and stop.

## Step 4.5 — Quality score

Read `quality` from that output.{% if _strict == 'block' %} `blocked: true` halts: give each `weak_dimensions` entry a fix and leave `status: draft`.{% else %} A low score only warns: print `weak_dimensions` and continue.{% endif %}

## Step 4.6 — spec-validator

One advisory pass, unless Step 0 skipped the interview with `irreversible_decisions: []`. {{ hm.dispatch("spec-validator", "with the SPEC, its machine.yaml and any RESEARCH doc; it returns JSON critiques") }}. It gates nothing: record the critiques under Open Questions, surface the critical ones, continue.

## Step 5 — Status and stamp

Set `status: approved` when Open Questions is empty, else `draft`. If the DRI chose "Approve this SPEC and end interview" and Step 4 passed, run `hm spec_machine approve --yaml specs/SPEC-<slug>.machine.yaml`. Else stamp `--exempt` only when `irreversible_decisions: []`, Step 4 passed, `status: approved`, and the DRI was not asked (`auto_full`). Else leave it unstamped.

Print the SPEC path, its status and `hm spec_machine approval-status --slug <slug>`, then STOP. `/hm:execute <slug>` is the user's call; if the world model began this run, enter it now unless its Advance rule stops.
